WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.083
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.383 --> 00:00:08.746
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.046 --> 00:00:14.996
Unit three: Animals & Habitats. In this unit, you will describe where animals live.

4
00:00:15.983 --> 00:00:16.833
Habitat.

5
00:00:17.533 --> 00:00:20.508
Habitat means the natural home of an animal or plant.

6
00:00:20.808 --> 00:00:23.028
The forest is the tiger's habitat.

7
00:00:23.728 --> 00:00:26.114
Your turn. Say: Habitat.

8
00:00:28.814 --> 00:00:29.768
Habitat.

9
00:00:30.783 --> 00:00:31.657
Jungle.

10
00:00:32.357 --> 00:00:35.633
Jungle means a thick, hot forest with many plants.

11
00:00:35.933 --> 00:00:37.724
Monkeys swing through the jungle.

12
00:00:38.424 --> 00:00:41.320
Your turn. Say: Jungle.

13
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:44.928
Jungle.

14
00:00:45.917 --> 00:00:46.720
Desert.

15
00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:50.035
Desert means a very dry place with little rain.

16
00:00:50.335 --> 00:00:52.056
Camels live in the desert.

17
00:00:52.756 --> 00:00:55.316
Your turn. Say: Desert.

18
00:00:58.016 --> 00:00:58.959
Desert.

19
00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:00.707
Ocean.

20
00:01:01.407 --> 00:01:04.266
Ocean means a very large area of salt water.

21
00:01:04.566 --> 00:01:06.090
Whales live in the ocean.

22
00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:08.827
Your turn. Say: Ocean.

23
00:01:11.527 --> 00:01:12.446
Ocean.

24
00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:14.056
Nest.

25
00:01:14.756 --> 00:01:17.418
Nest means a home that birds build for their eggs.

26
00:01:17.718 --> 00:01:19.636
The bird built a nest in the tree.

27
00:01:20.336 --> 00:01:23.023
Your turn. Say: Nest.

28
00:01:25.723 --> 00:01:26.655
Nest.

29
00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:28.372
Predator.

30
00:01:29.072 --> 00:01:31.490
Predator means an animal that hunts other animals.

31
00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:33.348
The lion is a predator.

32
00:01:34.048 --> 00:01:36.677
Your turn. Say: Predator.

33
00:01:39.377 --> 00:01:40.367
Predator.

34
00:01:41.383 --> 00:01:42.442
Coral reef.

35
00:01:43.142 --> 00:01:46.988
Coral reef means a colourful underwater place made by tiny sea animals.

36
00:01:47.288 --> 00:01:49.206
Many fish live on the coral reef.

37
00:01:49.906 --> 00:01:52.651
Your turn. Say: Coral reef.

38
00:01:55.351 --> 00:01:56.236
Coral reef.

39
00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.309
Savanna.

40
00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:02.321
Savanna means a large, flat grassland in a hot country.

41
00:02:02.621 --> 00:02:04.550
Zebras run across the savanna.

42
00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.380
Your turn. Say: Savanna.

43
00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:10.977
Savanna.

44
00:02:11.983 --> 00:02:12.717
Mammal.

45
00:02:13.417 --> 00:02:16.241
Mammal means an animal that feeds its babies milk.

46
00:02:16.541 --> 00:02:17.960
An elephant is a mammal.

47
00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:21.127
Your turn. Say: Mammal.

48
00:02:23.827 --> 00:02:24.631
Mammal.

49
00:02:25.617 --> 00:02:26.641
Reptile.

50
00:02:27.341 --> 00:02:31.639
Reptile means a cold-blooded animal with dry skin, like a snake.

51
00:02:31.939 --> 00:02:33.788
A crocodile is a reptile.

52
00:02:34.488 --> 00:02:36.896
Your turn. Say: Reptile.

53
00:02:39.596 --> 00:02:40.539
Reptile.

54
00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:42.354
Migrate.

55
00:02:43.054 --> 00:02:46.005
Migrate means to travel to another place each season.

56
00:02:46.305 --> 00:02:48.073
Some birds migrate in winter.

57
00:02:48.773 --> 00:02:51.065
Your turn. Say: Migrate.

58
00:02:53.765 --> 00:02:54.743
Migrate.

59
00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:56.763
Camouflage.

60
00:02:57.463 --> 00:03:00.020
Camouflage means colours that help an animal hide.

61
00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.354
The chameleon uses camouflage.

62
00:03:03.054 --> 00:03:06.136
Your turn. Say: Camouflage.

63
00:03:08.836 --> 00:03:09.895
Camouflage.

64
00:03:10.883 --> 00:03:12.894
Now let's listen to a conversation.

65
00:03:13.194 --> 00:03:15.240
Sreypich, where do lions live?

66
00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:18.387
Lions live on the savanna.

67
00:03:19.683 --> 00:03:20.835
And camels?

68
00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:25.336
Camels live in the desert. They don't need much water.

69
00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:27.930
What about fish?

70
00:03:29.217 --> 00:03:31.669
Many fish live on coral reefs in the ocean.

71
00:03:32.983 --> 00:03:36.167
Grammar focus: Present simple (facts).

72
00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:39.491
Lions live on the savanna. Fish live in the ocean.

73
00:03:39.791 --> 00:03:42.708
Use the present simple for facts that are always true.

74
00:03:43.717 --> 00:03:46.520
Now read and listen. Homes Around the World.

75
00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:49.028
Every animal has a habitat.

76
00:03:50.317 --> 00:03:53.408
Lions live on the savanna, while camels live in the desert.

77
00:03:54.717 --> 00:03:58.191
Monkeys live in the jungle, and colourful fish live on coral reefs.

78
00:03:59.483 --> 00:04:02.447
Birds build a nest to protect their eggs from predators.

79
00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:06.307
Some birds migrate to warmer places every year.

80
00:04:07.617 --> 00:04:10.141
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

81
00:04:10.441 --> 00:04:12.278
Camels blank in the desert.

82
00:04:12.578 --> 00:04:15.500
A, live. B, lives. C, living.

83
00:04:19.517 --> 00:04:21.481
The answer is A: live.

84
00:04:22.983 --> 00:04:25.401
An animal that hunts other animals is a blank.

85
00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:28.843
A, predator. B, mammal. C, nest.

86
00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:34.583
The answer is A: predator.

87
00:04:36.083 --> 00:04:38.245
Colours that help an animal hide are blank.

88
00:04:38.545 --> 00:04:42.419
A, camouflage. B, habitat. C, savanna.

89
00:04:46.417 --> 00:04:48.846
The answer is A: camouflage.

90
00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:54.581
Now it's your turn to speak. Which animal habitat is the most interesting to you?

91
00:04:59.881 --> 00:05:04.194
The coral reef is the most interesting to me. Thousands of colourful fish live there.

92
00:05:04.494 --> 00:05:06.830
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

93
00:05:07.817 --> 00:05:12.257
Great work today! You learned twelve new words and present simple (facts).

94
00:05:12.557 --> 00:05:17.009
Today's value is protecting wildlife. Protect animals and their homes.

95
00:05:17.309 --> 00:05:19.590
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

96
00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:22.449
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

